GATE 1 — WORK LIST.

Work list:     {{ .run_dir }}/evidence/worklist.md
Request:       {{ .run_dir }}/evidence/report.md
Run context:   {{ .run_dir }}/evidence/context.md
Evidence dir:  {{ .run_dir }}/evidence
  — everything else in this directory was put there by triage during
    discovery. It is what its claims must rest on.

Judge the work list. Do not execute it and do not rewrite it.

Check every claim about the current state against those artifacts. A
claim with nothing behind it was inferred from reading code, and a
plausible inference is not an observation.

On `worklist_approved`, your reason becomes the brief the executing
agent is launched with, and it is the only instruction that agent
receives. Write it as a directive, not as a verdict on the work list.

Remote-state changes: if the work list has a REMOTE CHANGES section,
that is the set of actions the executor may take outside this
worktree. It may take NONE of them unless your brief names them one
by one. Anything you do not name, it must report back instead of
doing. If an item needs an approval, a credential, or a decision that
is not yours, `needs_human` — do not delegate the judgement to the
executor by writing "do it if your token permits".

Call submit_outcome with `worklist_approved`, `worklist_revise`,
`worklist_reject`, or `needs_human`.